  <b>THE REFUSALS, IN THE DIALOG'S FOOTER</b>
  <color:#ef4444>A TAKEN CUT IS REFUSED.</color> That cut is taken and nobody has authorised it.
  The body is fixed and no run may price from it. The request waits on Market Risk.
  <color:#ef4444>AN INCOMPLETE BODY IS REFUSED.</color> That cut holds no complete body. The gaps
  are on the cut's page, and the take resumes once they are closed.
  <color:#ef4444>A REFUSED CUT IS REFUSED.</color> The authorisation was refused, and the remedy is a
  new take rather than a second decision.
  A SUPERSEDED CUT IS OFFERED: a rerun reproduces an earlier result from it, and the
  button says "anyway". No pin is needed, because a cut is a record of an instant.
  A CUT IN USE IS OFFERED, because its kind requires no authorisation: the take raised
  no request, so the body was usable when it was fixed. Where the kind fixes indicative
  values, as the flash kind does, every result priced from it carries the mark.
  [ Price from this cut ]
  --
