  <b>THE COMPARISON, IN THREE VERDICTS</b>
  <color:#22c55e>REPRODUCED.</color> One result computed twice: the same cut, the same engine, and
  every figure equal.
  <color:#ef4444>DIFFERS.</color> The body and the engine are the same and the result moved, which is a
  defect in the engine or in the code, and the first figure that differs is named.
  <color:#eab308>CANNOT BE COMPARED.</color> One of three reasons: the engine version differs, a part
  of the body is no longer served, or the body was retaken. An auditor writes it down.
